<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="ce16eb31">&lt;p&gt;
    The change plan needs to be integrated with the overall program plan and timing to take into account how and when the
    solution is introduced to stakeholders through communications and training.&amp;nbsp; The balancing act is having the
    solution ready for the people when the people are ready for the solution.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Timing estimates for accomplishing engagement, readiness and adoption activities needs to track with the overall
    program plan. If the change activity estimates exceed the overall program plan timeframes, then either the program plan
    needs to change its timeframes to accomodate what is needed for the engagement, readiness and adoption activities OR
    the engagement, readiness and adoption activities need to be scaled to fit the overall program plan timeframes, in
    which case potential implementation risks need to be identified.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="b8b29b58"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="dde26757"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="20546649">&lt;p&gt;
    Outline all change management activities and tasks, timeline, dependencies, resources and time estimates to execute the
    changes associated with implementing&amp;nbsp;the business solution.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Build commitment of sponsors and program leaders by getting them involved in deciding transition tactics.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Iterate&amp;nbsp;and consolidate into&amp;nbsp;the overall program&amp;nbsp;workplan.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
